Title: NO EXTRACTION
Credit: The Slice — Dialogue Script
Source: data/story/*.ts (sync with npm run script:check / script:import)
Draft date: 2026-11-10
Notes: Every spoken block ends with its line id as a note, e.g. [[c1.wren.open1]]. Keep the note when you rewrite a line.
    Parentheticals are the performance notes the VO actor sees. Cue extensions (RADIO), (PA), (RECORDING) are cosmetic.

# Chapter 1 — The Job

= Core Stability 72%. Ava live on the radio. Onboarding through the mission.

>CHAPTER 1 — THE JOB<

EXT. RIDGE ABOVE THE SABLE COMPLEX - NIGHT

Cinematic "The Job": a slow push down the valley to Ballast on the ridge.

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
(Calm, polite, corporate. Slight PA reverb.)
Halcyon Resource Group. Core Stability: seventy-two percent. All personnel proceed to assigned extraction points. Thank you for your service. [[c1.halcyon.core72]]

AVA (RADIO)
(Live radio. Brisk, warm under the professionalism.)
That's the broadcast. Seventy-two and falling. I'm holding the pad until oh-four-forty. [[c1.wren.open1]]

BALLAST
(Dry. An old joke between them.)
Not a minute after. [[c1.ballast.open1]]

AVA (RADIO)
Not a second after. Policy. Patrol below the ridge — keep your head down. [[c1.wren.open2]]

[OBJECTIVE] Infiltrate the Sable complex

[PROMPTS] WASD move · Mouse look — Hold Shift to sprint — Space vault low cover — Space climb

EXT. OUTER PATH - NIGHT

A lone trooper ahead.

AVA (RADIO)
(Quiet, focused.)
One trooper on the path. Get behind him. [[c1.wren.firstPatrol]]

[PROMPTS] C crouch — quieter, harder to see — F takedown — from behind, unaware targets

[OBJECTIVE] Take down the trooper

On his first takedown:

AVA (RADIO)
(Approving. A little proud. GDD-mandated line.)
Clean. Like always. [[c1.wren.clean]]

Further down the path, two troopers close together.

AVA (RADIO)
Two of them, close together. Drop the first and keep moving — you'll have a second before the other one knows. [[c1.wren.pair]]

[PROMPT] F again — chain takedown · [OBJECTIVE] Drop both troopers

On his first chain:

AVA (RADIO)
(Smiling.)
Two for two. Show-off. [[c1.wren.chainDone]]

EXT. COURTYARD - NIGHT

AVA (RADIO)
Courtyard ahead. Pulse your visor — their sightlines paint on the ground. [[c1.wren.visor]]

AVA (RADIO)
Cyan gate's the fast way in. It stays open as long as nobody knows you're there. [[c1.wren.fastGate]]

AVA (RADIO)
Or go around through the service yard. Slower. Safer. Your call. [[c1.wren.longRoute]]

[PROMPT] Q visor scan — marks enemies and their sightlines

[OBJECTIVE] Through the courtyard — cyan gate, or the service yard

EXT. INNER YARD - NIGHT

AVA (RADIO)
Spotter on the tower. Forty metres of eyes. Break his line, or take him off it. [[c1.wren.spotter]]

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
Seismic advisory. Personnel are reminded that extraction schedules are final. [[c1.halcyon.tremor]]

[OBJECTIVE] Reach the hangar

If he is spotted (alert reaches Hunted):

AVA (RADIO)
(Sharp. Worried, not panicked.)
They've got you. Break contact. [[c1.wren.seen]]

If the complex locks down:

AVA (RADIO)
Lockdown. Fast gate's sealed — hack the console or take the long way. [[c1.wren.lockdown]]

INT. HANGAR - NIGHT

Cinematic "FLAMINGO-07": reveal of the frame, then its face.

AVA (RADIO)
(A little awed.)
There she is. FLAMINGO-07. [[c1.wren.hangar1]]

BALLAST
(Deadpan.)
Big. [[c1.ballast.hangar1]]

AVA (RADIO)
Sable's planetary defense prototype. Pull the flight governor and she's the most expensive statue on Ilvane. [[c1.wren.hangar2]]

[OBJECTIVE] Pull the flight governor from FLAMINGO-07

He pulls the governor. The frame powers down.

BALLAST
(Genuinely a little sorry. GDD-mandated line.)
Sorry, big girl. [[c1.ballast.sabotage]]

AVA (RADIO)
Governor goes in the cargo tube. Policy: the part rides separate from the operative. [[c1.wren.tube]]

BALLAST
Policy says a lot of things. [[c1.ballast.tube]]

[OBJECTIVE] Drop the governor in the cargo tube

The governor drops. The rear gate opens. The extraction clock appears: 8:00.

AVA (RADIO)
(The clock appears on this line.)
Extraction window's open. Eight minutes. Pad's on the cliff. Don't make me wait. [[c1.wren.window]]

BALLAST
You've never waited for anyone in your life. [[c1.ballast.window]]

AVA (RADIO)
And I'm not starting tonight. Go. [[c1.wren.window2]]

[OBJECTIVE] Get to the extraction pad

EXT. OUTER GATE - NIGHT

AVA (RADIO)
Through the outer gate and you are out of their house. Keep going. [[c1.wren.exit]]

FADE OUT.

# Chapter 2 — Left Behind

= Core Stability 58%. Lockdown, the carbine, the first Timed Zone, the first cache.

>CHAPTER 2 — LEFT BEHIND<

EXT. MOTOR POOL - NIGHT

The extraction clock is still running.

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
Core Stability: fifty-eight percent. Extraction schedules are final. Halcyon thanks you for your patience. [[c2.halcyon.core58]]

AVA (RADIO)
(Urgent, still in control.)
They found the governor gone. The whole complex is waking up. Stay off their panels — if one of them reaches an alarm, every fast gate in the sector seals. [[c2.wren.alarm]]

BALLAST
Copy. Quiet. [[c2.ballast.alarm]]

AVA (RADIO)
Weapons rack by the motor pool. Sable carbine. Loud — anyone who hears it comes for you. [[c2.wren.carbine]]

AVA (RADIO)
(Knowing him.)
Armory's off the east road. Not on the way. If you're feeling greedy. [[c2.wren.armory]]

[OBJECTIVE] Cross the motor pool to the cliff road

[PROMPTS, contextual] Aurora flare — their radios and alarms are down for a few seconds — 1/2 swap — the carbine is loud — Fast gates sealed — hack a console or take the long way

Optional: in the armory he finds the missile rack.

BALLAST
Missile rack. Somebody's going to miss this. [[c2.ballast.missileRack]]

[OBJECTIVE] Follow the cliff road to the bridge

EXT. THE BRIDGE - NIGHT

He steps on. The bridge starts collapsing behind him. Timed Zone "The Pad" begins: 1:30.

AVA (RADIO)
(First crack of real worry.)
Ballast, the window's closing. Where are you? [[c2.wren.window]]

BALLAST
(Running, breathing hard.)
Bridge. Ninety seconds. Hold it. [[c2.ballast.bridge]]

[OBJECTIVE] Reach the pad

If the clock runs out:

BALLAST
Not like this. [[c2.ballast.bridgeFail]]

EXT. EXTRACTION PAD - NIGHT

Cinematic "Four Minutes Late": Ava's ship already climbing. Ballast alone on the pad.

AVA (RADIO)
(She hates every word.)
I can't. The window's closed. I'm lifting. Ballast, I'm— policy. I'm sorry. [[c2.wren.climbing]]

BALLAST
(Furious. Breathless.)
Ava. Ava! I am on the bridge! [[c2.ballast.wait]]

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
(Bleakly funny. Do not play it funny.)
Operative designation Ballast: credentials revoked. Evacuation complete. Personnel losses are within acceptable parameters. Thank you for your service. [[c2.halcyon.revoke]]

BALLAST
(Quiet. Disbelief.)
Four minutes. I was four minutes late. [[c2.ballast.pad1]]

BALLAST
(Talking back to the PA.)
Acceptable parameters. Sure. [[c2.ballast.pad2]]

The first major quake. The bridge behind him falls into the chasm.

BALLAST
(The ground goes out from under him.)
Oh, come on— [[c2.ballast.quake]]

[OBJECTIVE] The amber light — Ava left something

.PAD - AVA'S FIRST CACHE

Story cache 1. Plays as radio audio while he moves.

AVA (RECORDING)
(Recorded before lift-off. Steady, rehearsed, fragile underneath.)
If you're hearing this, I left. On schedule. You know the policy, and you know I follow it. [[c2.wren.cache1a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
Sable has one launch cradle left, at their yard. Past the dead colony, under the ice. I flew the route twice. I left you things along it. [[c2.wren.cache1b]]

AVA (RECORDING)
Amber light. You'll know. Don't make me regret this. [[c2.wren.cache1c]]

BALLAST
(To a recording that cannot hear him.)
You left me a voicemail. You left me a voicemail and a flashlight. [[c2.ballast.cache1reply]]

BALLAST
(Looking at the horizon.)
Sable's yard. Fine. Fine. [[c2.ballast.yard]]

FADE OUT.

# Chapter 3 — Dead Colony

= Core Stability 41%. The breacher, alternate routes, collapse events as tools, personal caches, the Freight Lift.

>CHAPTER 3 — DEAD COLONY<

EXT. COLONY STREET - SNOW

Cinematic "Dead Colony": a high shot down the empty street.

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
Core Stability: forty-one percent. Halcyon facilities on Ilvane are now unstaffed. Please do not contact Halcyon. [[c3.halcyon.core41]]

BALLAST
Dead colony. Of course it is. [[c3.ballast.open]]

[OBJECTIVE] Find a way through the colony to the freight lift

He picks up the breacher shotgun.

BALLAST
Breacher. Doors are a suggestion now. [[c3.ballast.shotgun]]

[PROMPT] Breacher opens weakened doors — loud

Near a weakened door:

BALLAST
(Hint: weakened doors open with the breacher.)
That door's had a hard week. [[c3.ballast.weakDoor]]

Near the leaning tower, troopers beneath it:

BALLAST
(Hint: lure them under it.)
That tower is coming down. Make it count. [[c3.ballast.collapseTool]]

[PROMPT] Shoot the tower's weakened leg with the breacher

EXT. PLAZA - SNOWSTORM

Debris falls across the plaza. It hits Sable too.

[OBJECTIVE] The radio mast — then the freight building

.RADIO MAST - AVA'S SECOND CACHE

AVA (RECORDING)
The colony has been empty six days. Sable pulled out and left their own people at the mast. I bounced this off it. [[c3.wren.cache2a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
The freight lift goes down to the core conduits — the only way under the ridge. And the cargo never shipped, Ballast. Everything we sent down the tube is stuck in that shaft. Including your souvenir. [[c3.wren.cache2b]]

BALLAST
My governor. You sent me back for my own governor. [[c3.ballast.cache2reply]]

[TOAST] Route marked · [OBJECTIVE] Freight lift — north of the plaza

.OFF-ROUTE - PERSONAL CACHE 1

Optional. Points to the flight governor.

AVA (RECORDING)
(Personal. Softer.)
This one's not on the route. You always check the corners. I thought you'd find it. [[c3.wren.pc1a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
Cargo bay in the lift shaft. If you want that frame to fly instead of hop, the governor's in there. The shaft floods when the pumps go. Be fast. [[c3.wren.pc1b]]

BALLAST
Fly instead of hop. Noted. [[c3.ballast.pc1reply]]

.OFF-ROUTE - PERSONAL CACHE 2

Optional.

AVA (RECORDING)
(Remembering. Almost laughing.)
Remember Kessel Station? You carried me two kilometres because I said my ankle was fine. [[c3.wren.pc2a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
It wasn't fine. You knew. You didn't say anything. You never say anything. [[c3.wren.pc2b]]

BALLAST
…It was three kilometres. [[c3.ballast.pc2reply]]

INT. FREIGHT BUILDING

[OBJECTIVE] Take the freight lift down

He steps on the car. It groans and descends.

BALLAST
Going down. [[c3.ballast.liftDown]]

INT. LIFT SHAFT - CARGO BAY

Timed Zone "Freight Lift" begins: 3:00. The water rises with the clock.

BALLAST
(Timed Zone start.)
Pumps are failing. Water is coming up the shaft. [[c3.ballast.freightLift]]

[OBJECTIVE] Release both hatch locks before the bay floods

Optional: he finds the flight governor in the cargo.

BALLAST
(To the governor.)
Hello again. [[c3.ballast.governor]]

After the first lock: [OBJECTIVE] One more hatch lock. After both: [OBJECTIVE] Through the conduit hatch.

With under 30 seconds left (reuses the Chapter 4 line):

BALLAST
Water's rising. [[c4.ballast.water]]

If the bay floods:

BALLAST
Too slow. Again. [[c3.ballast.liftFlood]]

He gets through the hatch.

FADE OUT.

# Chapter 4 — Under the Ice

= Core Stability 24%. Darkness and the visor, Heavies, Hounds, the Conduit Flood.

>CHAPTER 4 — UNDER THE ICE<

INT. CONDUIT TUNNELS - DARK

Only a dim helmet lamp.

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
(Barely audible, through ice.)
Core Stability: twenty-four percent. This is an automated message. There is no one left to receive your call. [[c4.halcyon.core24]]

BALLAST
Can't see a thing. Visor it is. [[c4.ballast.dark]]

[PROMPT] Q visor scan — in the dark, it is how you see

[OBJECTIVE] Follow the conduits toward the yard

.TUNNEL - AVA'S THIRD CACHE

AVA (RECORDING)
Under the ice is Sable's conduit network. It runs to their forward depot, right under the yard. [[c4.wren.cache3a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
The core is bleeding into the water down there. If it starts rising, don't think. Run. [[c4.wren.cache3b]]

BALLAST
Don't think. Run. Your best advice in eleven years. [[c4.ballast.cache3reply]]

[OBJECTIVE] Through the pump hall

INT. PUMP HALL

A Heavy patrols.

BALLAST
Heavy. Don't trade with that. Get behind it. [[c4.ballast.heavy]]

[PROMPT] Heavies are armoured in front — takedown from behind

INT. MAINTENANCE BAY - PERSONAL CACHE 3

Optional. Points to the arc blade.

AVA (RECORDING)
Maintenance bay, past the pump hall. Sable keeps frame tools there. [[c4.wren.pc3a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
There's an arc blade on the rack. You always liked getting close. Don't get too close. [[c4.wren.pc3b]]

BALLAST
Little late for that. [[c4.ballast.pc3reply]]

He takes the arc blade.

BALLAST
Arc blade. Sorry, Sable. [[c4.ballast.arcBlade]]

INT. THE RUNS

Hounds.

BALLAST
(Whispered.)
Hounds. They hunt by sound. Walk. [[c4.ballast.hounds]]

[PROMPT] Hounds hunt by sound — walk, crouch, or throw a decoy (T cycle, G throw)

.OFF-ROUTE - PERSONAL CACHE 4

Optional. The one she was afraid to record.

AVA (RECORDING)
(Very quiet. This is the one she was afraid to record.)
Last one. I nearly didn’t leave it. [[c4.wren.pc4a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
They named you Ballast because you're the weight they drop so the ship can rise. I never called you that. Not once. [[c4.wren.pc4b]]

AVA (RECORDING)
(Ballast’s real name, said once.)
Come home, Teo. [[c4.wren.pc4c]]

BALLAST
…Nobody's called me that in a long time. [[c4.ballast.pc4reply]]

INT. MAIN CONDUIT

Timed Zone "Conduit Flood" begins: 2:30. The water front chases him.

BALLAST
Water's rising. [[c4.ballast.water]]

BALLAST
(Conduit Flood start.)
Here it comes. [[c4.ballast.conduit]]

[OBJECTIVE] Outrun the water

INT. FORWARD DEPOT

Cinematic "The Forward Depot": he looks up.

BALLAST
(He sees FLAMINGO-07.)
Forward depot. And— no way. [[c4.ballast.depot]]

FADE OUT.

# Chapter 5 — Flamingo

= Core Stability 11%. Flamingo's voice arrives: the first thing in hours that answers him.

>CHAPTER 5 — FLAMINGO<

INT. FORWARD DEPOT

Cinematic "FLAMINGO-07": the frame, parked and dead.

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
(Nothing else. The script has run out of comfort.)
Core Stability: eleven percent. [[c5.halcyon.core11]]

BALLAST
(Hand on the frame.)
They couldn't fly you out. Because of me. [[c5.ballast.aegis]]

[OBJECTIVE] The amber light by the frame

.DEPOT - AVA'S LAST STORY CACHE

AVA (RECORDING)
If you made it this far, you found her. They left her behind because she can't fly. Because of you. [[c5.wren.cache4a]]

AVA (RECORDING)
The yard has one cradle left. Sable's ace is guarding it — they call him the Marshal. You're going to need the frame. [[c5.wren.cache4b]]

BALLAST
I know. I know. [[c5.ballast.cache4reply]]

[OBJECTIVE] Board FLAMINGO-07

INT. FLAMINGO-07 COCKPIT

Cinematic "Boot-up", unskippable. All audio ducked. His breathing.

If he recovered the flight governor in Chapter 3:

BALLAST
(Reinstalling the flight governor.)
Undoing my own work. Great. [[c5.ballast.install]]

[READOUT] FLAMINGO-07 // COLD START

FLAMINGO-07
(System voice: precise, unhurried, not human, not cold.)
FLAMINGO-07. Cold start. [[c5.aegis.boot1]]

[READOUT] REACTOR ........ NOMINAL / HYDRAULICS ..... NOMINAL

FLAMINGO-07
Reactor nominal. Hydraulics nominal. [[c5.aegis.boot2]]

[READOUT] PILOT AUTHORIZATION ......

FLAMINGO-07
Pilot authorization… rejected. [[c5.aegis.boot3]]

[READOUT, red] PILOT AUTHORIZATION ...... REJECTED

BALLAST
(Ripping a panel. Manual bypass.)
Yeah. I figured. [[c5.ballast.bypass]]

[READOUT] …MANUAL

FLAMINGO-07
…Manual. [[c5.aegis.boot4]]

[READOUT] FLAMINGO-07 ONLINE. The cockpit floods with light. Control returns mid-line.

FLAMINGO-07
(Control returns mid-line.)
FLAMINGO-07 online. [[c5.aegis.boot5]]

Flamingo reports the loadout he found. With the governor:

FLAMINGO-07
Flight governor installed. Sustained flight available. [[c5.aegis.governorOk]]

Without it:

FLAMINGO-07
Flight governor absent. Jump jets only. [[c5.aegis.governorMissing]]

If he took the missile rack:

FLAMINGO-07
Shoulder rack armed. [[c5.aegis.missileOk]]

With the arc blade:

FLAMINGO-07
Arc blade armed. [[c5.aegis.bladeOk]]

Without it:

FLAMINGO-07
Melee: manipulator shove. [[c5.aegis.noBlade]]

EXT. THE YARD

The first enemy dies within four seconds of control.

BALLAST
(First enemy dies within four seconds of control.)
Okay. Okay. I get it now. [[c5.ballast.firstKill]]

A Warden squad arrives. [OBJECTIVE] Erase the Warden squad

BALLAST
(Predator now.)
Wardens. I've been hiding from you for two days. [[c5.ballast.wardens]]

SABLE
That's Flamingo. Who is flying Flamingo? [[sable.warden.aegis]]

[OBJECTIVE] Repair station, then the shelf. At any repair station:

FLAMINGO-07
Repair station: armor restored. [[c5.aegis.repair]]

EXT. ICE SHELF

Timed Zone "Shelf Run" begins: 1:30. The shelf breaks up behind him.

FLAMINGO-07
(Shelf Run start.)
Ice integrity failing. Recommend: speed. [[c5.aegis.shelf]]

BALLAST
Boost. Boost! [[c5.ballast.shelf]]

[OBJECTIVE] Assault boost across the shelf (hold boost) · [PROMPT] Hold Shift — assault boost

If the clock runs out:

BALLAST
Too slow. [[c5.ballast.shelfFail]]

EXT. MAGNETIC STORM

FLAMINGO-07
Magnetic storm. Targeting offline. Manual aim. [[c5.aegis.storm]]

[OBJECTIVE] Survive the storm. When it clears:

FLAMINGO-07
Targeting restored. [[c5.aegis.stormEnd]]

[OBJECTIVE] Through the canyon

EXT. CANYON - AMBUSH

Short cinematic: Wardens on the cliff. A hit tears off his left arm.

FLAMINGO-07
Left arm lost. Rifle transferred to right mount. [[c5.aegis.armLost]]

BALLAST
That was my good arm. [[c5.ballast.arm]]

[OBJECTIVE] Repair, then the launch platform

EXT. LAUNCH PLATFORM

Cinematic "The Marshal": the cradle, then his frame, SOVEREIGN. Open channel.

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
(Open channel. Professional, tired, respectful.)
Halcyon. You stole the one thing on this rock I was told to protect. [[c5.marshal.intro1]]

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
My people are on that cradle. It lifts on my word. You're not getting on it. [[c5.marshal.intro2]]

BALLAST
Your people left you here too. [[c5.ballast.marshal1]]

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
I know. That's the job. [[c5.marshal.intro3]]

[BOSS] SOVEREIGN

Phase 1. Sometimes, when their blades meet:

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
Good. You fly like you mean it. [[c5.marshal.p1]]

Whenever he charges his overcharge beam:

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
(Overcharge beam.)
Hold still. [[c5.marshal.beam]]

UNUSED — written, never triggered:

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
There it is. [[c5.marshal.hit]]

Phase 2. The platform ring collapses. Warden support arrives.

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
Platform's breaking. Neither of us has long. [[c5.marshal.p2]]

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
Wardens, on me. Last time, I promise. [[c5.marshal.p2support]]

Phase 3. He grapples Flamingo and rips the shoulder cannon off.

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
(The grapple.)
Give me that cannon. [[c5.marshal.p3]]

FLAMINGO-07
Shoulder cannon lost. [[c5.aegis.cannonLost]]

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
Now we're even. [[c5.marshal.p3b]]

EXT. LAUNCH PLATFORM - AFTER

Cinematic "One of Us": SOVEREIGN fallen.

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
(Dying, calm.)
Cradle's yours, Halcyon. [[c5.marshal.death1]]

THE MARSHAL (RADIO)
(His last line. Acknowledges Ballast as the one who got out.)
One of us should get out. Go on. Get out. [[c5.marshal.death2]]

BALLAST
…Thanks. [[c5.ballast.marshalDead]]

FLAMINGO-07
Launch cradle locked. Booster armed. [[c5.aegis.cradle]]

[OBJECTIVE] The cradle. He locks in.

FADE OUT.

# Chapter 6 — Ascent

= Core Stability 2% to 0%. Climb, strip, break atmosphere, the planet, Ava, the final line.

>CHAPTER 6 — ASCENT<

EXT. LAUNCH CRADLE

HALCYON SYSTEMS (PA)
Core Stability: two percent. Halcyon Resource Group thanks you for your service. [[c6.halcyon.core2]]

[OBJECTIVE] Climb

FLAMINGO-07
Booster ignition. [[c6.aegis.launch]]

BALLAST
(Under 4G.)
Come on. Come on— [[c6.ballast.launch]]

[PROMPT] WASD steer clear of the debris

.THE CLIMB

Debris hits. The frame is too heavy to make orbit.

FLAMINGO-07
Hull damage. Mass too high for orbit. [[c6.aegis.damage]]

Jettison 1, at 18% of the climb:

FLAMINGO-07
Jettison: weapons. [[c6.aegis.jettisonWeapon]]

BALLAST
Take it. Take all of it. [[c6.ballast.jettison1]]

Jettison 2, at 38%:

FLAMINGO-07
Jettison: shoulder assembly. [[c6.aegis.jettisonShoulder]]

Jettison 3, at 60%:

FLAMINGO-07
Jettison: armor. [[c6.aegis.jettisonArmor]]

BALLAST
(Almost a laugh. He finally owns the name.)
Dump the weight. That is what I am for. [[c6.ballast.jettison3]]

Jettison 4, at 82%:

FLAMINGO-07
Booster stage separation. [[c6.aegis.jettisonBooster]]

Past 96%:

FLAMINGO-07
(The last thing before silence.)
Atmosphere: exited. [[c6.aegis.atmo]]

INT. COCKPIT - ORBIT

Cinematic "You're Late", unskippable. Total silence.

BALLAST
(In the silence. Barely breath.)
…Huh. [[c6.ballast.drift]]

Cut to the planet. Ilvane breaks apart. Core Stability: 0%.

Cut to a ship approaching. Ava's.

AVA (RADIO)
(Live again. Through static. She came back.)
—allast. Ballast, come in. I've got your beacon. I turned around. [[c6.wren.return]]

Back to the cockpit.

BALLAST
(Final line. Dry. Exhausted. One take.)
…You’re late. [[c6.ballast.final]]

If he found all four personal caches, the same line plays as a warmer take (c6.ballast.final.warm).

SMASH CUT TO BLACK.

>THE END<

==

# Sable Barks

= Random per situation, 90-second cooldown per line. Never comic, occasionally human.

.SABLE BARKS - IDLE

SABLE
Still no seat number. Third night running. [[sable.idle.seats]]

SABLE
If your name's not on the manifest, you're on the shelf. That's what they said. [[sable.idle.manifest]]

SABLE
My sister made the second lift. I think. Comms were down. [[sable.idle.sister]]

SABLE
Last ship goes when the Marshal says. Not before. [[sable.idle.lastship]]

SABLE
Heard Halcyon left half their people. Heard we're doing the same. [[sable.idle.rumor]]

SABLE
Can't feel my hands. Can't feel the ground stop shaking either. [[sable.idle.cold]]

SABLE
They keep doing headcount. Like the number is going to go up. [[sable.idle.count]]

SABLE
You can see the yard from here. Doesn't look any closer. [[sable.idle.yard]]

SABLE
They said the next shuttle. That was four days ago. [[sable.idle.shuttle]]

.SABLE BARKS - SUSPICIOUS

SABLE
What was that? [[sable.sus.what]]

SABLE
Movement. Hold on. [[sable.sus.movement]]

SABLE
Checking it. Stay on comms. [[sable.sus.checking]]

SABLE
…Could be the wind. Could be. [[sable.sus.wind]]

.SABLE BARKS - HUNTED

SABLE
Contact! Contact! [[sable.hunt.contact]]

SABLE
Halcyon operative! He's real! [[sable.hunt.halcyon]]

SABLE
Flank him! Don't let him reach the gate! [[sable.hunt.flank]]

SABLE
There! On the ice! [[sable.hunt.there]]

.SABLE BARKS - LOST TARGET

SABLE
